Local Anomaly Detection and Classification

Purpose: The purpose of this package is to identify and classify anomalies in time series data. 

Installation:
1. Clone this gitHub repostiory by:
git clone https://github.com/claudiamrk/localanomaly.git 

Install the package using:
devtools::install()

Then load the package:
library(localanomaly)

Required Input

The package is designed for time-series data containing:

time: the time/date of each observation
value: the numerical value observed at that time

For example:

time                  value
2026-01-01 00:00:00   18.2
2026-01-01 01:00:00   18.5
2026-01-01 02:00:00   18.7

The specific dates and values are not required; this is an example of the expected structure

Implemented Functions:

1. clean_data():

Purpose:
Cleans and prepares the input time-series data for anomaly detection.

How to check

clean_data(data)

This functions checks that the input is in the correct format which is a date column that is in POSIXct format and 
has a value corresponding to this date.
The expected input is therefore a dataframe that has a date column in this POSIXct format and a value for each date.
The function will stop and return the relevant error for any non numerical input or if there is no time date included, 
in the incorrect format or insufficient amount of observations. 

find_neighbours() and local_statistics() are designed to receive the validated outputs 
from the functions in the workflow before it. Therefore, invalid raw input formats are not expected at this stage,
as input validation is handled by clean_data()

2. find_neighbours():
Purpose:
Finds the neighbouring observations for each observation in the time series. 
The number of neighbours is determined based on the size of the input dataset.

How to check:

find_neighbours(data)

The function should return the neighbouring observations for each observation in the dataset.

3. local_statistics():

Purpose:
Calculates local statistics for each observation based on its neighbouring observations.

The function calculates the local:
mean
standard deviation
minimum
maximum

How to check:
local_statistics(data, neighbours)

The function should return the calculated local statistics for each observation.


